  "narrative": "Riverside Retail is genuinely shrinking, not seasonally dipping: revenue is down 16.5% to \u20b9146,919 a month with a consistent two-year downward slope. The order pattern shows more, smaller orders (average order value down 43.4%), suggesting the customer is splitting spend elsewhere rather than buying less of one thing. This is broad-based and structural, not tied to any single category or price change.",
  "attributed_categories": [],
  "cited_evidence": [
    "Monthly revenue fell 16.5%, from a baseline of \u20b9175,870 to a recent rate of \u20b9146,919, a drop well outside this account's normal swing.",
    "Revenue in the second half of the account's history ran 18.9% below the first half, with a steady month-on-month decline since September 2024.",
    "Average order value dropped 43.4%, from \u20b9155,742 to \u20b988,151, even as order frequency rose 42.7% and basket width fell 30%, pointing to smaller, more scattered orders.",
    "No single category stopped buying; declines are spread across six of eight categories including Power Tools, Precision Hardware, Diagnostic Equipment and Consumables.",
    "Margin held steady at 29.0% to 29.2% and average discount barely moved (4.8% to 5.1%), so the loss is not coming through price or discounting."
  ],
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Contact the account to understand why orders are smaller and more frequent, a possible multi-sourcing signal.",
    "Investigate the disappearance of the Cordless Drill 18V and Cutting Blade 10pk products.",
    "Escalate as whole-account disengagement to the account manager rather than a single-category fix."
  ],
